{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread","id":975383,"title":"Preview Documents Discussion Thread!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-23T22:55:37-07:00","id":975383,"title":"Preview Documents Discussion Thread!","content":"So, since we have the Early Access teaser, the Theoi writeup, and now we have <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/scion-2nd-edition-tabletop-rpg/posts/1689871?ref=activity\" target=\"_blank\">a preview for the intro fiction</a>, I think we could use a dedicated thread to just talk about things we noticed, liked, and things that don't QUITE fit in the &quot;Questions about the teaser core&quot; thread.<br /> <br /> Among all the things I love (seriously, my only complaint so far is that it might take me a bit of time to fully grok the combat), there's ONE thing that really jumped out at me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Example: Officers Jud and Nicky might interrogate a suspect together, allowing one of them to roll Presence + Persuasion while the other rolls their own dice pool and adds the result as an<br /> Enhancement. Alternatively, Jud might go to check on forensics with Reason + Intelligence while Nicky asks the questions on her own. </div> </div> </div>Wait a minute... Cops... Jud and Nicky...<br /> <br /> Jud and Nicky...<br /> <br /> ... Judy and- <i>Oh you clever bastards</i>!<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://vignette2.wikia.nocookie.net/disney/images/0/03/Nick_and_judy_zootopia_renders.png/revision/latest?cb=20151220130400\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T23:06:07-07:00","id":975386,"title":"","content":"I don't have specific examples right now because work has utterly fried my brain, but the FATE and Powered by the Apocalypse influence all over the game shine clear and are objectively good in my eyes. If the Investigative mode draws on GUMSHOE, the giddiness might make me faint! I <i>adore</i> how simple but deep Paths are, as they neatly handle things usually represented through a cumbersome combination of GM fiat and merits/feats/whatever in other games.<br /> <br /> My only complaint is that we don't have character creation to gawk over; I think being able to spit out some mortals to generate discussion would help generate discussion and an early understanding of Storypath.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T01:58:35-07:00","id":975430,"title":"","content":"I really love the Path system. I can't begin to describe how awesome it is. I like the idea of Momentum. The weapon tag system is easy to remember and cool. The idea behind Complications and Consolation are really cool. Scale seems like a really interesting idea, and I want to see more about it.<br /> <br /> The only two notable downsides are the taking damage stress and injury complication system. That's a hot mess. And Loki is not a fire god, so that has me a little worried.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T02:51:12-07:00","id":975445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=975430#post975430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Loki is not a fire god, so that has me a little worried.</div> </div> </div> </div>The explanation for why he is is quite neat, though, because it obliquely references the reason that he was believed to be a fire god for a long time (Loki/Logi).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4855-eggs-maledict","name":"Eggs Maledict","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T03:34:17-07:00","id":975457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eggs Maledict</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=975445#post975445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The explanation for why he is is quite neat, though, because it obliquely references the reason that he was believed to be a fire god for a long time (Loki/Logi).</div> </div> </div> </div>But it's wrong. It was a mistake. Why embrace it? Unless the reference is supposed to be tongue in cheek and a bit of comedy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T04:27:30-07:00","id":975466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=975457#post975457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it's wrong. It was a mistake. Why embrace it? Unless the reference is supposed to be tongue in cheek and a bit of comedy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's a nod to the fact that mortal belief does influence the gods of the World to a certain degree. <br /> <br /> Speaking of, I think it's freaking awesome that they're adding in narrativist RPG Elements- what better for a game about playing the heroes of modern day sagas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T05:44:32-07:00","id":975480,"title":"","content":"I was about to address the Nemean Elephant in the room before I saw this thread. Yes, there is so much of FATE in this game, I half expected us to roll 4dF for resolutions.<br /> I do, like the OP, think that these pieces from other systems are a rather good thing. These bits of rules allow for a more 'sense of wonder' design aesthetic - it is far easier, with what I've seen of this new system, to handle the gonzo action sequences that arise in Scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T09:18:29-07:00","id":975548,"title":"","content":"Gotta say, I like Eileen in the fiction. Can't wait to see the rest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12349-evilnerf","name":"evilnerf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12349_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T09:32:46-07:00","id":975556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evilnerf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=975548#post975548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gotta say, I like Eileen in the fiction. Can't wait to see the rest.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I get the fiction correctly she is a PRE visitation scion who had something running with a scion of morrigan?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T09:39:05-07:00","id":975559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=975556#post975556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I get the fiction correctly she is a PRE visitation scion who had something running with a scion of morrigan?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, they've said elsewhere that she's a Scion of Dagda. So my guess is this piece of fiction is about her visitation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12349-evilnerf","name":"evilnerf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12349_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T09:47:24-07:00","id":975562,"title":"","content":"I wish I had access to a computer that could take the standard site as well as the forums, this one just throws up an error every time.<br /> <br /> From what I'm hearing here though it sounds good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=975430#post975430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea behind Complications and Consolation are really cool. Scale seems like a really interesting idea, and I want to see more about it.<br /> <br /> The only two notable downsides are the taking damage stress and injury complication system.</div> </div> </div> </div>*looks at bookshelf* so should I be filing this alongside my Fate books instead of my World of Darkness books?<br /> <br /> Fate does stress and consequences/injuries, and it works really well. I'm not sure how well it'll work here, it took Fate a few tries to get it right (seriously SotC, 5 basic Stress Boxes? Considering that many actions won't be attacks that's long combats), but I suspect that the forum will have worked out decent values within a week of backer pdfs going out. The entire idea of the system is to have a short buffer that refills about every scene, and then consequences/injuries to let you fight longer, and if you get it right it works, depending on the combat people will either risk taking a few consequences (in Fate your Major consequence can stay with you for the entire campaign if you're unlucky, so it's not always something to do lightly) or will concede once they're out of stress.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PHGraves</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=975480#post975480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was about to address the Nemean Elephant in the room before I saw this thread. Yes, there is so much of FATE in this game, I half expected us to roll 4dF for resolutions.<br /> I do, like the OP, think that these pieces from other systems are a rather good thing. These bits of rules allow for a more 'sense of wonder' design aesthetic - it is far easier, with what I've seen of this new system, to handle the gonzo action sequences that arise in Scion.</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as there's something similar to Create an Advantage and Situation Aspects I'm fine. Those two tools can replace hundreds of pages of systems for various things, including combat techniques, political plays, planning, teamwork, and so on. I personally love Fate (I keep starting attempts to translate WoD and CofD to it), so a heavy Fate influence will just make my inevitable system conversion easier (although I'll need the books because the one thing I'll admit is that OP writes better fluff than I do).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T10:02:53-07:00","id":975570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evilnerf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=975559#post975559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, they've said elsewhere that she's a Scion of Dagda. So my guess is this piece of fiction is about her visitation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also my guess there (didnt know that that was her the scion of dagda). Especially with &quot;your dad wants to talk&quot;^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T10:13:17-07:00","id":975571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=975562#post975562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as there's something similar to Create an Advantage and Situation Aspects I'm fine. Those two tools can replace hundreds of pages of systems for various things, including combat techniques, political plays, planning, teamwork, and so on. I personally love Fate (I keep starting attempts to translate WoD and CofD to it), so a heavy Fate influence will just make my inevitable system conversion easier (although I'll need the books because the one thing I'll admit is that OP writes better fluff than I do).</div> </div> </div> </div>There are, it seems. Stunts (spending extra threshold successes above difficulty) can create Enhancements for your friends or Complications for your enemies. There's also Fields, which are bundles of situational Enhancements or Complications. There's also Conditions, which work very much like temporary Aspects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T10:45:35-07:00","id":975591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=975571#post975571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are, it seems. Stunts (spending extra threshold successes above difficulty) can create Enhancements for your friends or Complications for your enemies. There's also Fields, which are bundles of situational Enhancements or Complications. There's also Conditions, which work very much like temporary Aspects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems overly complex. Part of the beauty of Situation Aspects is that the term covered everything, and thanks to the Fate Point economy theoretically anyone could benefit from them. I mean, I don't know how the system here works, it could be as awesome as tuna on pizza or as horrible as wasabi-flavoured prawn crackers, I'll judge them when I see the full rules, but I wonder what the problem with having them all be the same thing, just attached to something else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T10:49:15-07:00","id":975596,"title":"","content":"Tuna on Pizza, never had it, but concider me intrigued.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T11:22:21-07:00","id":975613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=975596#post975596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tuna on Pizza, never had it, but concider me intrigued.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, people look at me weird when I order a seafood pizza (generally contains tuna and prawns, as well as a few other things). It's one of those things that sounds weird, but I got to like it because for a long time my big sister would only eat pizza if it was cheese and tomato or seafood. Although I also love fish, so that might have something to do with it.<br /> <br /> I do recommend trying it, but it's not something for everyone. There's actually a lot more to pizza than what people think, another one I like is where you get a thin crust with no sauce, top it with spinach, sprinkle some salt on it and crack an egg in the middle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T11:32:02-07:00","id":975620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=975457#post975457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it's wrong. It was a mistake. Why embrace it? Unless the reference is supposed to be tongue in cheek and a bit of comedy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they wanted to introduce the concept of a god stealing the mantle of another","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T14:15:43-07:00","id":975693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=975430#post975430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only two notable downsides are the taking damage stress and injury complication system. That's a hot mess. And Loki is not a fire god, so that has me a little worried.</div> </div> </div> </div>He wasn't back in the ninth century, he is now. The text even tells you what went down on the divine side while mortals were confusing Loki with Loge in text.<br /> <br /> There's also the issue of Loki's parents who being lightning (Farbauti) and leaves (Laufey) or pine needles (Nal), would imply an association with wildfire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T15:00:52-07:00","id":975703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=975613#post975613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, people look at me weird when I order a seafood pizza (generally contains tuna and prawns, as well as a few other things). It's one of those things that sounds weird, but I got to like it because for a long time my big sister would only eat pizza if it was cheese and tomato or seafood. Although I also love fish, so that might have something to do with it.<br /> <br /> I do recommend trying it, but it's not something for everyone. There's actually a lot more to pizza than what people think, another one I like is where you get a thin crust with no sauce, top it with spinach, sprinkle some salt on it and crack an egg in the middle.</div> </div> </div> </div> I hate most fish, but love Tuna, and Pawns and shimp freak me out, too many legs, you might as well be eating bugs or at least that's what the dark recesses of my brain tell me.<br /> <br /> But Tuna mixed with more traditional ingrediants like peperoni, assorted ground meats, cheeses, bacon, ham, sausage would be great. I love Tuna, but I rescently found I like Tuna with BBQ sauce as well which likely seems weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T06:46:09-07:00","id":975925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=975613#post975613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, people look at me weird when I order a seafood pizza (generally contains tuna and prawns, as well as a few other things). It's one of those things that sounds weird, but I got to like it because for a long time my big sister would only eat pizza if it was cheese and tomato or seafood. Although I also love fish, so that might have something to do with it.<br /> <br /> I do recommend trying it, but it's not something for everyone. There's actually a lot more to pizza than what people think, another one I like is where you get a thin crust with no sauce, top it with spinach, sprinkle some salt on it and crack an egg in the middle.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>[B</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Omegaphallic[/B]]I hate most fish, but love Tuna, and Pawns and shimp freak me out, too many legs, you might as well be eating bugs or at least that's what the dark recesses of my brain tell me.<br /> <br /> But Tuna mixed with more traditional ingrediants like peperoni, assorted ground meats, cheeses, bacon, ham, sausage would be great. I love Tuna, but I rescently found I like Tuna with BBQ sauce as well which likely seems weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bPersonal favorite: Bacon, Pineapple, Jalapeno, in that ratio. Salty, sweet, and some heat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T13:25:48-07:00","id":976072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=975693#post975693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He wasn't back in the ninth century, he is now. The text even tells you what went down on the divine side while mortals were confusing Loki with Loge in text.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Loki fire thing will get you teased in academic circles. Like thinking Loki is Thor's brother because of Marvel.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=975693#post975693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also the issue of Loki's parents who being lightning (Farbauti) and leaves (Laufey) or pine needles (Nal), would imply an association with wildfire.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, the connection between Farbauti and lighting was completely fabricated back around 1880ish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T14:30:13-07:00","id":976101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=976072#post976072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Loki fire thing will get you teased in academic circles. Like thinking Loki is Thor's brother because of Marvel.<br /> As far as I know, the connection between Farbauti and lighting was completely fabricated back around 1880ish.</div> </div> </div> </div>And in Scion, Loki is liable to set you on fire out of annoyance and trying to take one of his finest moments from him purely because you're a stickler for literally ancient history.<br /> <br /> He explicitly absorbed the original fire god in this world a long time ago, his parentage's Purviews is unimportant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T14:32:09-07:00","id":976103,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to resign myself to the fact that Scion is not going to be 100% accurate, and I think everyone will have an easier time if they do the same. Now if you'll excuse me, I need to mope about the various Netjer mergers for a little while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T14:34:23-07:00","id":976104,"title":"","content":"It seems like the smallest thing in the world to un-merge any fan's given sacred cow, never mind the notion that we don't have a full understanding of mantling and how that can affect individual gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T15:34:15-07:00","id":976123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=976101#post976101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And in Scion, Loki is liable to set you on fire out of annoyance and trying to take one of his finest moments from him purely because you're a stickler for literally ancient history. He explicitly absorbed the original fire god in this world a long time ago, his parentage's Purviews is unimportant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a lot of people play this game because of the mythology. It's just really strange that they would use fan fiction versions as the baseline instead of the mythology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2447,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","user":"TwitchTheRat","date":". 09-25-2016, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T15:38:10-07:00","id":976127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=976123#post976123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that really Loki, though? Or a fan fiction?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's apparently Loki in Scion. Whether Scion can be called &quot;fan fiction&quot; or not sort of sidesteps the issue that like 99% of mythology qualifies as fan fiction about the gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T15:38:50-07:00","id":976128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=976123#post976123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that really Loki, though? Or a fan fiction?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering, as with Greek myth, all the Norse myth we have comes by way of entertainment storytellers, not some religious canon, that distinction is nonexistent. Pretending otherwise is the height of pedantry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T15:50:44-07:00","id":976130,"title":"","content":"To be clear, I would be mildly disappointed if Loki was always the fire God and they just unquestioningly accepted the historic error. But that's not what they did. The wove the error into its own new story to show how Loki has changed since the Ninth Century. That's cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T16:00:03-07:00","id":976133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=976127#post976127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's apparently Loki in Scion. Whether Scion can be called &quot;fan fiction&quot; or not sort of sidesteps the issue that like 99% of mythology qualifies as fan fiction about the gods.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=976128#post976128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering, as with Greek myth, all the Norse myth we have comes by way of entertainment storytellers, not some religious canon, that distinction is nonexistent. Pretending otherwise is the height of pedantry.</div> </div> </div> </div>And neither of you feel like there is a difference between paying some respect to the stories we all grew up loving, and just making something up wholesale? I just don't want this to turn into another Scion 1st Edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T16:14:56-07:00","id":976141,"title":"","content":"I don't see them as completely sacrosanct. There's nothing wrong with adding stuff about what they've been up to since their respective heydays.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T16:16:02-07:00","id":976142,"title":"","content":"There's no point in doing new stories with the gods if the gods aren't allowed to do new shit. Loki tricking Loge into devouring himself and stealing his mantle sounds 100% in character with the Loki I grew up with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T16:37:57-07:00","id":976161,"title":"","content":"If y'all want 100% accurate gods, go ahead and post revisions on the forum. Those who care will use them and/or debate the subtleties and nuances of mythology with you, and the rest of us can use the gods as-is without worrying that the deities in question are going to sue us. At the end of the day, it's a game for fun among friends, and if we can get past how Christianity is portrayed in some anime, we can get through this with a deep breath and a smile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T16:44:32-07:00","id":976164,"title":"","content":"I don't really have a horse in the race of the portrayals in Scion vs the source material because I'm no student of mythology. The writers of the system are probably bigger mythology geeks than I.<br /> <br /> Though I vaguely recall hearing some notes of the whole &quot;Accurate myths&quot; thing is... Well, accurate to what? And to when?<br /> <br /> Like, the whole Loki as a Fire God thing... Sure, it might be true that Loki originally wasn't a Fire God.<br /> <br /> But after a certain point, people started saying he was. So which is more accurate?<br /> <br /> To me, the whole &quot;Loki <i>wasn't</i> a Fire God, but did after an incident in this point in history that matches to when people historically started thinking of him as a Fire God-&quot; sounds good enough for my table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T20:42:29-07:00","id":976328,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=976128#post976128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Considering, as with Greek myth, all the Norse myth we have comes by way of entertainment storytellers, not some religious canon, that distinction is nonexistent. Pretending otherwise is the height of pedantry.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">this is especially true. The various myths didn't have one specific source. The norse were not a united people, nor where most faiths. Even the empires that were united such as Rome or Egypt had numerous different stories and myths of the various gods. After all look at the Theoi and how they changed and evolved over the centuries as the Greeks grew and expanded their city states to the empire of Alexander and his successors and to the Romans.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Anyways as this is about preview documents some things I noticed in the Theoi Section. I will also preface this by saying I actually worship them IRL, so I might have different views then others and this was just my opinion of things when I read it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Aphrodite:</b> I like this for the most part.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Eldest of the Theoi:</b> that is not a title I have ever heard for Aphrodite. Now I have heard that title but it is for Hestia, who in most myths was the first olympion to be born.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Apollo:</b> I really like this write up.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Ares</b>: Overall I like this little write up for the most part.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Why does Ares not like drone warfare?</b>: If one looks at the damage drones cause and America's use, then it is certainly destructive. Not sure why Ares would hate Drones in particular if he was fine with all other technology improvements. So perhaps a sentence on why he doesn't like drones in Scion?</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Ares and Veterens</b>: In the little write up there was nothing about Ares and veterans. I would assume that there would be something on how Ares regards Veteran affairs?</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Women Soldiers</b>: As the god of war, there wasn't a comment on women's soldiers in modern militaries.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Artemis</b>: I like the write up here. the Modern day has plenty of story seeds which is good.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Athena</b>: I like her write up for the most part. Particular the story seed of corruption in democracy annoying her.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Demeter</b>: Generally I like this.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Modern hunger</b>: In the comment about how people are still hungry despite her gifts. Perhaps a line about how she tries to help and motivate people to alleviate it in whatever ways she can?</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Dionysus</b>: Again mostly liked though one thing stood out.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Theater</b>: Dionysus is the God of Theater among the Theoi. One of the bigger festivals for Dionysus was the Greater Dionsyia, which could be viewed as religious event + theater festival. There should be Some about that and how he views modern Theatre and movies.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Hades: </b>Generally good.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Digging for gold: </b>It seems like the sentence about digging into the earth for gold was cut short? In any case it isn't that clear on what he thinks of those digging into the earth for gems and minerals.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Modern world:</b> While I get the impression of a tired Hades in the Modern world, beyond that there isn't much story seeds here that pop. I would like to see more of his view on the modern world. </span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Hephaestus:</b> Another one that I quite like.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Hera: </b>This is probably the only writeup that I actually didn't like.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Hera and Zeus:</b> I know the general view is that Hera does not really liking Zeus, but from all the different myths I don't really get that impression. She doesn't like his cheating and has a famous fury, yet, despite this she does love him. While there are a number of stories of them fighting, it ends with them making up.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Hera and Marriage:</b> As someone who does worship the Theoi. I generally see Hera as supportive of Marriages made for love. After all a Marriage that is made out of love is a marriage that isn't likely to break. That is important to her. More over I see her quite in favor of Gay Marriage. That is a fight for marriage, and yet this write up comes off as she isn't carrying about one of the bigger successes in one of her central purview.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Women: </b>She is Queen of the Gods, as such one of her principal things she looks over are women. She is far more then just the goddess of Marriage, though that is her major role. I would assume that there would be a few sentences in the modern day on the changing role of women. If anything she would be supportive IMO of women taking charge in the mortal world as well as helping to care for women's issues.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Her Agency:</b> Overall this section reads for me as if Hera has little agency of her own. That isn't true in the slightest. Most of her furies are her own, more over she also aides heroes in their own quests. Most famously she helped Jason and the Arognauts in their quest for the Golden Fleece. This ties into the first comment about her relationship to Zeus. She sticks with Zeus because <i>SHE</i> wants to. The Modern day section also didn't feel like there were any story seeds here.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Hermes: </b>I quite like this one. I particularly like the relationship implied between Hermes and Thoth.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Hestia:</b> A decent one though a few things.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Home Goddess:</b> She is the Goddess of Hearth and Home, not sacrifice as sacrifices to the theoi is the central act of worship. Would like to see a bit more in the Modern day section on the modern home for Hestia.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Persephone:</b> Another decent one.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Poseidon:</b> I like this one. It should be noted droughts are one of the things he is known to afflict on those that wrong him. Perhaps mention some modern droughts like the California drought as perhaps his ire?</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Zeus:</b> this one was meh to me. Now I didn't come away disliking it but hey this is for improvements.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Zeus and Hera:</b> I mentioned a good bit in the Hera Section. So not to repeat myself. I regard Zeus as loving Hera the most of all the women. He may sleep with other women and have affairs but he reserves his heart for her despite all their fights and make ups and fights.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>the King of the Gods:</b> Zeus is the King of the Gods, as part of that he is the god of Law and Order. Hence why oaths were made in his name. I would like to see more in this write up as his role as the King of the Gods, particularly in the Modern world.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Modern world: </b>Aside from the comment on numerous Scions there is not much to go on how he regards the modern world. Particularly America, which can be seen as the spiritual successor to Rome.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Religion:</b> Now I am not sure on the setting atm, but judging from this I am going to assume that either 1.) the religion surived underground somehow in the age of monotheism. Or 2.) the polythesitic religions of Hellenismos and Religio Romana expericed a huge revival. I really want to know more on how it survived despite the Roman empire stamping it out. </span></span><ul><li><b>Olympic Games:</b><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Nothing mentioned on the Olympic Games which were festivals and games in the ancient world dedicated to Zeus Olympus, and there were other games for other gods such as the Haraea Games for Hera. However being as how big the Olympic games are in the modern world, perhaps a sentence or two about them?</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Hellenismos: </b>It mentions two of the major mystery cults as 'religions' without actually mentioning the faith that worships them in the modern world?</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Sacrifice:</b> No mention in the Religion section about basically the central act of worship to the theoi(and most polytheistic faiths tbh) of Sacrifice, which includes votive and libations, and perhaps some challenges/non-challanges that faces in this setting.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Relationships:</b></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>The two relationships:</b> it was a little unclear at first that the two main relationships were the Annua and the Netjer. So perhaps the first sentence about it could read something like: \u201cThe Theoi have historical ties to two major pantheons \u2013 the Netjer in Egypt and the Annua in the middle east.\u201d ?</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Motif</b>: A neat little paragraph, though Perhaps this should be at the front of the chapter?</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">All in all though, I did like the write up for the Theoi. I would like to see some sample characters here but I assume that comes later? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T21:52:09-07:00","id":976348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>herkles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=976328#post976328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Why does Ares not like drone warfare?</b>: If one looks at the damage drones cause and America's use, then it is certainly destructive. Not sure why Ares would hate Drones in particular if he was fine with all other technology improvements. So perhaps a sentence on why he doesn't like drones in Scion?</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>My guess? Where's the soldiering in piloting a drone? If you're going to kill a man, at least be there so you can see him drop dead from your bullet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T22:38:41-07:00","id":976364,"title":"","content":"Weighing in late, because of stupid time zone differences and a stupid need to not get fired from my job for following this with the rapt interest that I'm currently following it with.<br /> <br /> We kind of all have a horse in this race; We're all fans of legend and mythology. That's why we play, and it's really nice for the narrative and the people in it to be as factual as possible. It's cool to interact with a &quot;big guy who can cast lightning&quot;. It's really, <i>really</i> cool to be interacting with Thor in all his red-bearded, ham fisted glory. It's more immersive, and you're not thrown out of the moment with jarring inconsistencies.<br /> <br /> On the other hand Scion, as an RPG, <i>is</i> fan fiction. No pantheon I know of (and I'm happy to be corrected) has stories of progenitor creation-deities waking up/escaping into the modern day with the intention to destroy it all or remake it all in their own image. The moment that's the premise of the game then things are already different to how they factually are. Not to mention doing what any other fan fiction does, and inserting your own character. It's already 'not the same'. It's even less so with your character in it. And some of the modern gods have changed their patterns, behaviours, and in some cases &quot;their thing&quot;. Twitch is right; hard core scholars are likely to look funny at you for mixing up Loki and Loge. But Glamourweaver's also got a good point. Loki, on deciding to interact with the world in a more meaningful way, stealing someone else's mantle is in character. So is the thematic fallout at the end of it, where he comes to his usual sticky end for over-reaching.<br /> <br /> There's some give and take needed. Or some houserules for a reasonably simple fix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2608,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","user":"Squee","date":". 09-26-2016, 01:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T22:43:23-07:00","id":976366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>herkles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=976328#post976328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[FONT=arial]<br /> snip</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bGreat post, herkles, especially in regards to your comments about Hera and Zeus' relationship. Even from what little I know of Greek Myth those two's marriage is a lot more dynamic than angry, spiteful harridan and unfaithful abuser. Those elements are still there of course, but Hera and Zeus do actually love each other to some extent and its kind of inaccurate to ignore that, even with viewing them from a modern lens.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T22:54:32-07:00","id":976370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Squee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=976364#post976364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weighing in late, because of stupid time zone differences and a stupid need to not get fired from my job for following this with the rapt interest that I'm currently following it with.<br /> <br /> We kind of all have a horse in this race; We're all fans of legend and mythology. That's why we play, and it's really nice for the narrative and the people in it to be as factual as possible. It's cool to interact with a &quot;big guy who can cast lightning&quot;. It's really, <i>really</i> cool to be interacting with Thor in all his red-bearded, ham fisted glory. It's more immersive, and you're not thrown out of the moment with jarring inconsistencies.<br /> <br /> On the other hand Scion, as an RPG, <i>is</i> fan fiction. No pantheon I know of (and I'm happy to be corrected) has stories of progenitor creation-deities waking up/escaping into the modern day with the intention to destroy it all or remake it all in their own image. The moment that's the premise of the game then things are already different to how they factually are. Not to mention doing what any other fan fiction does, and inserting your own character. It's already 'not the same'. It's even less so with your character in it. And some of the modern gods have changed their patterns, behaviours, and in some cases &quot;their thing&quot;. Twitch is right; hard core scholars are likely to look funny at you for mixing up Loki and Loge. But Glamourweaver's also got a good point. Loki, on deciding to interact with the world in a more meaningful way, stealing someone else's mantle is in character. So is the thematic fallout at the end of it, where he comes to his usual sticky end for over-reaching.<br /> <br /> There's some give and take needed. Or some houserules for a reasonably simple fix.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess the issue is the automatic assumption that &quot;fan fiction&quot; is a bad or subpar thing, which is far from the truth. Or that being fanfiction in the first place is somehow qualitatively different from the mythology in question.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T22:58:59-07:00","id":976374,"title":"","content":"True that.<br /> <br /> RP is all about fan fiction. What if <i>your</i> Jedi was in the Rebel Alliance? What if your Grey Warden was active during the events of the first Dragon Age game? That's what makes it awesome.<br /> <br /> But on the other hand I can't deal when someone makes grand sweeping changes to 'what's right' either so I can see it from the other side too. Tell me Loki bogarted Fire and I'll be all 'Cool. Hehehehe. That rascal.'. Tell me the Greek deities go 'Roman' and form one big conglomerate pantheon with the Egyptians and I'll go 'No. I can't swallow that.'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T00:17:59-07:00","id":976404,"title":"","content":"I've liked most of what I've read so far, although admittedly I need to read it a bit more closely. I like that they sort of addressed the Dionysos vs Hestia debate in her section, leaving it open for her to be one of the Dodekatheon even if most tend to assume that Dionysos has her spot. I'm curious what her other Calling will be, though. I'm a bit surprised that they didn't give Athena Artistry (Weaving), though, given that craftwork was one of her major spheres of influence. Still, that's an easy house rule to implement, so I suppose I should let it go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T00:33:43-07:00","id":976409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=976142#post976142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no point in doing new stories with the gods if the gods aren't allowed to do new shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that what our games are for? I feel like the books should give us a baseline that is somewhat accurate, and then we are the ones who tell the new stories at our table. Published adventures and modules excluded of course.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Squee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=976364#post976364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We kind of all have a horse in this race; We're all fans of legend and mythology. That's why we play, and it's really nice for the narrative and the people in it to be as factual as possible. It's cool to interact with a &quot;big guy who can cast lightning&quot;. It's really, <i>really</i> cool to be interacting with Thor in all his red-bearded, ham fisted glory. It's more immersive, and you're not thrown out of the moment with jarring inconsistencies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you phrased this so much better than me. For me, it's a jarring inconsistency and isn't really Loki. Now I never said it was a big deal all by itself. It was just something that has me a little worried. The worry comes from wondering how many other gods are going to get the same treatment. If enough inconsistencies pile up, then we are back into 1st Edition territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T01:01:48-07:00","id":976416,"title":"","content":"The myths would change as time passed and humans changed - that just makes sense. Now, if Tezcatlipoca becomes God of Bards, and Artemis suddenly starts sleeping around with men, then I'll worry. If something in the write-up bugs you that much [i.e. Fire God Loki], then leave it as it was. But I'd be frustrated if they brought the religions of the old Gods up to the 21st Century, and assumed that nothing had changed in the interim. Maybe it stays static in our Abrahamic faiths, because the teachings are dogma and the Gods don't appear to interfere in the world [by which I mean God/Allah/Jehovah doesn't come down and address the U.N. in our world, which Odin could do exactly that in Scion 2nd Edition's world], but why would it stay exactly the same if the deities constantly have new adventures, have Scions elevated to God status, and manipulate human societies? Bring on the reasonable additions and tweaks; we're all going to change stuff as we play anyway!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T01:32:38-07:00","id":976423,"title":"","content":"I actually really enjoyed a little web-series called the O-Cast, about the Greek gods coming to the world and 'trying to fit in'. It's a little wacky and comedic for how I would prefer a game of Scion to be run but I would love to see the theme of the gods returning to the world and trying new things and marvelling at how what they really dig on has changed. Not to say that they ditch the old way of doing things (they're gods. They're perfect as they are, damn it!) but the idea of Apollo staring at Hendrix playing the Star Spangled Banner and going &quot;Man, where do I get one of <i>those</i>?&quot; kind of appeals to me too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T13:04:03-07:00","id":976682,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Regarding the Loki-as-fire-God debate: I distinctly remember reading that the sound of crackling fire had been described as &quot;Loki beating his children&quot; in later folklore.<br /> Also, check this out: <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Linux Libertine\">The expressions: &quot;Lokke (Lokki) s\u00e5r havre i dag&quot; (Lokke (Lokki) sows oats today), or: &quot;Lokke driver i dag med sine geder&quot; (Lokke herds his goats today), are used in several regions of Jutland, for example in Medelsom shire, the diocese of Viborg</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Linux Libertine\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> etc. ... and stand for the sight in the springtime, when the sunshine generates vapour from the ground, which can be seen as fluttering or shimmering air in the horizon of the flat landscape, similar to the hot steam over a kettle or a burning fire&quot;<br /> Also, how about Lokabrenna (Loki's bonfire/burning) as an old name for Sirius?<br /> So, one could say His connection to fire is not entirely baseless. <br /> After all, in the world of legend binary thinking just doesn't work. Loki travels through air, He changes shape (and sex), He creates chaos that helps support a world order He is not entirely a part of, He is there at humanity's creation and one of the central figures of Ragnarok - why assume Lodur can't be a fire God just because at a certain point He enters a contest with another being representing fire? Whether it was there originally, or developed over time, the association is very much valid.<br /> Not to mention the fact that His personality and ambivalent role can so easily be symbolized through the beauty and danger of flame,that the metaphor is just irresistible.<br /> Legend and poetry have much in common, so whatever feels true might very well be true in both.<br /> </span></span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T06:48:46-07:00","id":977151,"title":"","content":"As a pagan follower of the Norse gods, I feel like I need to chime in on the Loki fire discussion as well. <br /> <br /> Historical accuracy is nice and everything, but the problem is that it ignores the fact that Norse paganism is still practiced today, and seeing as how we largely had to rebuild our religion from the ground up, it was inevitable that things would be lost in translation and get changed.<br /> <br /> Who cares that the ancient Norse didn't actually associate Loki with fire? Modern Norse pagans do. It may have started because of a misunderstanding, but at this point it's taken on a life of its own. Are you going to tell me that all these active followers of Loki associating him with fire wouldn't begin to give him an association with fire? Times have changed, and if you ask modern pagans, the gods have changed too. <br /> <br /> And what better accomplishment for the God of Lies than to gain a new purview based on a lie. If that's not one of Loki's greatest tricks, then I don't know what else to tell you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9296-zeldafan42","name":"Zeldafan42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9296_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T09:06:01-07:00","id":977203,"title":"","content":"<b>Scion 2e</b> has to juggle what the ancients thought of their gods, what modern worshippers think of their gods, the needs of a role-playing game, the needs of popular culture, and the idea that the Gods of <b>Scion</b> are largely singular entities who change both by their own impetus and due to Fatebinding over time.<br /> <br /> We're striving a lot for accuracy, but it's a secondary concern. A very important secondary concern, but still secondary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T09:48:17-07:00","id":977811,"title":"","content":"I want to say that Storypath alone has me intrigued, and the Scion previews have me digging through old issues of Hellboy to construct BPRD-alikes and such.<br /> <br /> I'll be following this with interest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T15:00:25-07:00","id":979870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>herkles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=976328#post976328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[LIST][*]<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Aphrodite:</b> I like this for the most part.</span></span>[LIST][*]<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Eldest of the Theoi:</b> that is not a title I have ever heard for Aphrodite. Now I have heard that title but it is for Hestia, who in most myths was the first olympion to be born.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Well I can say that Aphrodite is considered the eldest in the Symposium, but that is a bunch of philosophers being playful. They all tell stories with their own way to make an ode to Love (Aphrodite) They reason she must be the eldest because Love (Their definition being looser than ours) must have come first for there to even be a Universe. <br /> <br /> As for Accuracy vs Not. The truth is that while accuracy is important, the nature of the game (if we are to tell modern stories) are the gods existing in a modern world and affected by the stories told. It would be more odd for the Gods not to grow towards their real myth. I mean, unless we insist that they only exist in their eldest forms (and thus not pantheons at all but warring gods representing different factions of the tribes/clans/city states nearby.) The truth is the myths we do have organically changed over time to fit the needs and beliefs of the cultures that worshiped them. A modern story of mythology must acknowledge that history changes Gods. One wanes and another gains pre-eminence, they travel, and yes, they change. If modern myths change then it makes sense that at least some part of them might acknowledge those myths. Why do their stories change who is related to whom? Why is Zeus not the same as Jupiter? <br /> <br /> I feel that is every bit as much part of mythology as the stories themselves, and that is at the core of telling modern myths. Of course that can only be done by respecting the original myths, but Loki being a Fire God is respectful and told respectfully as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T15:08:01-07:00","id":979876,"title":"","content":"Well, a story about Aphrodite's origin is that she was born from the sea foam where Cronus cut off Uranus' genitals and hurled them into the ocean. This predates the six children of Cronus and Rhea by a noticeable bit. The other origin is that she was born to Zeus and Dione. So by one origin, she <i>is</i> the eldest of the Olympians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T15:13:10-07:00","id":979881,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but in the Symposium at least they portrayed her older even than them, making her the absolute first in creation above the others. The way it's written up, I felt they were referencing this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T16:03:57-07:00","id":979900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=979881#post979881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but in the Symposium at least they portrayed her older even than them, making her the absolute first in creation above the others. The way it's written up, I felt they were referencing this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Symposium IIRC, differentiates the two origins as different goddesses, one of heavenly platonic (original meaning) love, one of earthly lust.<br /> <br /> In Scion terms Aphrodite Urania and Aphrodite Pandemos would be different Mantles.<br /> <br /> Personally I favor the Zeus &amp; Dione origin, because it would explain the otherwise startling lack of myths where Zeus and Aphrodite hook up (or Zeus assaults Aphrodite). If she's his daughter, that's pretty consistent with the other myths where that's the one type of incest that does appear taboo to the Olympians (Orphic legend of Zagraeus as child of Zeus and Persephone being a Mystery Cult outlier).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T16:18:30-07:00","id":979913,"title":"","content":"I actually agree with you completely, I've always had a soft spot for the Symposium so I'd probably use both, but I've always viewed Aphrodite as the daughter of Zeus. But the great way Scion was written up allows for all mantles to be true/relevant and I'm looking forward to this aspect a great deal. Especially when it comes to Egyptian mythos where a lot of interesting mantles have been taken at various times. I mean if all the creation myths happened, I feel there can be multiple mantles of Aphrodite of various age and parentage...<br /> <br /> Which I think kinda proves my point about the accuracy issue. We have several Aphrodite s of various parentage and myth, all effected by history and cultural perceptions. If that isn't proof enough that some mantles have to at least be acknowledged in a modern setting as still evolving ie Loki and fire, I don't know what is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T22:18:43-07:00","id":980097,"title":"","content":"Am I the only one that got a chuckle about the fact that in a pantheon full of gods killing, torturing, or turning people into spiders or statues or (anything else under the sun), it's Hephaestus trying to embarrass his cheating wife and her lover, and as I recall, being laughed at by the other gods at least as much, if not more than Aphrodite and Ares, that gets called out as vindictive?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T22:58:28-07:00","id":980118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=980097#post980097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I the only one that got a chuckle about the fact that in a pantheon full of gods killing, torturing, or turning people into spiders or statues or (anything else under the sun), it's Hephaestus trying to embarrass his cheating wife and her lover, and as I recall, being laughed at by the other gods at least as much, if not more than Aphrodite and Ares, that gets called out as vindictive?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's probably in reference to the throne he constructed for Hera specifically to torture her. In revenge for her abandoning him as an infant for being crippled by throwing him off Olympus (to be fair for this point, keep in mind the Theoi are 100% immortal save for two odd exceptions, so this isn't <i>quite</i> as bad as it sounds) he constructs an insanely elaborate throne that he sends up to Olympus as a gift for Hera.<br /> <br /> Hera sits upon this grand, beautiful throne, and it springs around her entombing her within the throne by invisible fetters. As the throne was constructed from adamant, no one could free her, so they had to go find the craftsman. Hephaestus refused to free his mother (keep in mind this is a culture where Matricide and Patricide, and all sorts of attacks upon a parent are seen as <i>incredibly-incredibly</i> bad) until the Theoi send Dionysus down to earth to get him absolutely wasted, where he agrees to free Hera in exchange for one of the thrones of the Dodekatheon.<br /> <br /> So, are the Theoi vengeful? Yes, it's a defining trait. But, Hephaestus is absolutely vengeful to the nth degree in their context of societal hate for crimes against one's parent. He also made that throne out of adamant, and almost <i>nothing</i> is made of that, only the most important and powerful things. So, Heph put a <i>lot</i> of time, and effort into his vengeance.<br /> <br /> Oh, and add to the 'crimes against the parent' angle that this is also a case of crimes against royalty, which are also pretty bad. Add to <i>all</i> of that, that the Greeks don't care what your parents did to deserve it, all that matters is you <i>dared</i> violate the sacred bond between parent and child. That gets Nemesis or The Furies after you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T01:03:37-07:00","id":980149,"title":"","content":"Well said line came immediately after the sentence about the classic netting story. It also doesn't say the Theoi specifically think he's vindictive. It just states that he's vindictive in general. When I'd classify him as one of the three nicest in the pantheon along with Hades and Persephone. I can't recall any of the three straight up murdering anyone off the top of my head...<br /> <br /> Honestly I understand the comment, I just found it amusing that the brother that skinned a guy alive for challenging him to a rock off and tricked his sister into murdering the one guy she ever liked out of jealousy, as just one of the many examples of the Greek gods being terrible people, doesn't get the title but &quot;plays mean spirited tricks on people that are mean to him&quot; does. Just one of the funny little hypocrisies that make them some of my favorite mythological figures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T14:21:55-07:00","id":980426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=979870#post979870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Accuracy vs Not. The truth is that while accuracy is important, the nature of the game (if we are to tell modern stories) are the gods existing in a modern world and affected by the stories told. It would be more odd for the Gods not to grow towards their real myth. I mean, unless we insist that they only exist in their eldest forms (and thus not pantheons at all but warring gods representing different factions of the tribes/clans/city states nearby.) The truth is the myths we do have organically changed over time to fit the needs and beliefs of the cultures that worshiped them. A modern story of mythology must acknowledge that history changes Gods. I feel that is every bit as much part of mythology as the stories themselves, and that is at the core of telling modern myths. Of course that can only be done by respecting the original myths, but Loki being a Fire God is respectful and told respectfully as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you have to look at it as a kind of currency. There is no reason <b>not</b> to be accurate unless you are trading that accuracy for something important, so you always want to ask yourself <b>&quot;What am I getting in return?&quot;</b><br /> <br /> In the case of Loki, we can say that the important thing we gained is the demonstration of a god gaining the mantle of someone else, and a smooth way of addressing the controversy in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T16:04:05-07:00","id":980459,"title":"","content":"Loki stole Logi's mantle by tricking him into eating himself. Now i'm picturing him trying to do the same thing with Poseidon<br /> &quot;So You're telling me my wife hid my favorite Trident Polisher inside a pool of acid?<br /> &quot;Yep! Just swin and grab it you're the god of the sea no way you'd drown in acid <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> &quot;Ah, okay My trident is kinda dirty...<br /> OHHHH SHIT&quot;<br /> &quot;Yay,got him now to bang his wife... *Shapeshiftes into a woman* &quot;Lesbian style!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions"