kin' about dude stuff.<br /> <br /> Maybe they're drinking mead? That'd be fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T09:33:58-07:00","id":982171,"title":"","content":"After watching The Almighty Johnsons, all I really want is for Ullr to be included with the Aesir so I can make a Scion who always wins at games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9296-zeldafan42","name":"Zeldafan42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9296_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T08:24:28-07:00","id":982705,"title":"","content":"I just wanna say I only just got pointed to the Knacks Preview and am <i>super</i> happy with what I saw there. Making the capacities of the characters something innate - rather than coin-operated - delights me. I would really like some more Knack previews, to be honest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T14:20:39-07:00","id":983527,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B01LwCGSbE8kZDNGdDBWaVJZX2M/view\" target=\"_blank\">We got the Tuatha now.</a><br /> <br /> I would comment on it, but I'm too busy digesting this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Domnu, Mother of Titans</b><br /> .<br /> Whether she literally birthed the Titans or her role is more symbolic, Domnu is Danu's counterpart and a mysterious lord of the deep. She stokes the fires of resentment in her offspring, scheming to overthrow the Tuatha and become the mother of a new Irish pantheon.<br /> <br /> Purview: Darkness. Virtues: <b>Fecundity, Submission.</b> </div> </div> </div>Guys, don't look now, but I think the queen of the Fomorians is a horny anime maid,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 10-07-2016, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T16:42:23-07:00","id":983595,"title":"","content":"So while I love the content, I'm a bit surprised to see Danu with only three Purviews. In 1st edition the number of Purviews and Epic Attributes was, if not a direct representation of how powerful gods were, close enough (since they represented level 11 in the specific power). Is this still the case in 2nd ed? If not, why does Danu get less than pretty much any god or goddess seen so far, being one of if not the most important goddess in the pantheon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T16:54:36-07:00","id":983599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=983595#post983595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So while I love the content, I'm a bit surprised to see Danu with only three Purviews. In 1st edition the number of Purviews and Epic Attributes was, if not a direct representation of how powerful gods were, close enough (since they represented level 11 in the specific power). Is this still the case in 2nd ed? If not, why does Danu get less than pretty much any god or goddess seen so far, being one of if not the most important goddess in the pantheon?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the answer is that a tradeoff was made in favor of game balance over accurate representation of divine power levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T17:01:09-07:00","id":983603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=983595#post983595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So while I love the content, I'm a bit surprised to see Danu with only three Purviews. In 1st edition the number of Purviews and Epic Attributes was, if not a direct representation of how powerful gods were, close enough (since they represented level 11 in the specific power). Is this still the case in 2nd ed? If not, why does Danu get less than pretty much any god or goddess seen so far, being one of if not the most important goddess in the pantheon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps those are just the Purviews she is most familiar with and she has others,but that's not explained here cause the fine workings of a gods power is still being planned?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T17:06:42-07:00","id":983608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=983595#post983595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So while I love the content, I'm a bit surprised to see Danu with only three Purviews. In 1st edition the number of Purviews and Epic Attributes was, if not a direct representation of how powerful gods were, close enough (since they represented level 11 in the specific power). Is this still the case in 2nd ed? If not, why does Danu get less than pretty much any god or goddess seen so far, being one of if not the most important goddess in the pantheon?</div> </div> </div> </div>The impression I'm getting from 2nd edition is that gods get the purviews that are most iconic to their legends, and everything secondary gets relegated to their Callings, or something gods can do because they possess divine skill. Lugh has all the Epic Attributes, but doesn't have the War purview despite leading the Tuatha in battle. Instead, he gets the Warrior and Leader callings. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T17:07:04-07:00","id":983609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guitarsniper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=983599#post983599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think the answer is that a tradeoff was made in favor of game balance over accurate representation of divine power levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's honestly a flaw in the system (at least in first edition). There are very eclectic gods who are not top tier and very focused gods who are.<br /> <br /> Odin shouldn't drastically outclass Zeus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T18:05:32-07:00","id":983653,"title":"","content":"I don't know about the actual mythological backing, but I'm a little bummed to see The Dagda not have Death to suggest his resurrection powers that I've at least seen in some other media. I was banking on having a Dagda/Anpu war over the sanctity of the dead!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T18:17:59-07:00","id":983658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=983653#post983653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know about the actual mythological backing, but I'm a little bummed to see The Dagda not have Death to suggest his resurrection powers that I've at least seen in some other media. I was banking on having a Dagda/Anpu war over the sanctity of the dead!</div> </div> </div> </div>True resurrection (as opposed to the undead) might actually fall under Health. Not that he has that either (that's Dian Cecht's dominion for the Tuatha)<br /> <br /> It's been stated the purview spread is the most changeable aspect of the document still, so things are potentially up in the air still. I noticed Brighid doesn't have Forge despite that explicitly being one of her three aspects (the other two being the Hearth and the Fire of Inspiration)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 10-07-2016, 09:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T18:43:59-07:00","id":983669,"title":"","content":"I did notice that it seems like five is the max number of associated Purviews that Gods seem to get in the new Edition. The Theoi, the Tuatha? They all have between 3-5 Purviews associated with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T18:55:58-07:00","id":983675,"title":"","content":"Well if something has to budge I'd argue that Forge is more central to Brighid than either Health or Sun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T19:02:48-07:00","id":983676,"title":"","content":"Semi-related: Thanks for the pronunciation guide. Apparently I've been pronouncing practically everything wrong.<br /> <br /> I <i>have</i> been pronouncing Mananann mac Lir correctly though, so yay me","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T20:40:49-07:00","id":983727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=983675#post983675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well if something has to budge I'd argue that Forge is more central to Brighid than either Health or Sun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always got the impression that Health was a pretty strong aspect of Brigid. The whole caregiver third of the trio. (And I have a selfish reason of wanting to make a Scion of Brigid who is mostly a healer.) Sun, though, while I think it's cool, never seemed a big thing to me.<br /> <br /> I agree the pronunciation guide is nice. A lot of people (most people?) aren't familiar with irish spelling. I had to spend a few weeks reading through some irish myths with a pronunciation guide of my own at my side, sounding out every name I came across, before I felt remotely comfortable sounding things out on the fly. And I still half-ass it half the time. (It doesn't help that old irish spelling doesn't follow the same rules as modern irish.) Before that concerted effort I was pronouncing almost everything wrong too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T20:51:48-07:00","id":983736,"title":"","content":"Well I have relatively little trouble with them, I do hope the Teotl get a pronunciation guide for everyone who struggless with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T20:54:42-07:00","id":983738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=983727#post983727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always got the impression that Health was a pretty strong aspect of Brigid. The whole caregiver third of the trio. (And I have a selfish reason of wanting to make a Scion of Brigid who is mostly a healer.) Sun, though, while I think it's cool, never seemed a big thing to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I stand by what I said about the importance of Forge being above both, but I'd agree Health outranks Sun, and can tie into her Hearth-Mantle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T23:09:46-07:00","id":983775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=983738#post983738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I stand by what I said about the importance of Forge being above both, but I'd agree Health outranks Sun, and can tie into her Hearth-Mantle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's odd... The writeup even mentions that Brigid forges wonders for the Tuatha, but she doesn't have Forge as a purview.<br /> <br /> Nor does <i>any</i> of the Tuatha, near as I can tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T23:21:10-07:00","id":983779,"title":"","content":"Brighid needs Forge, definitely. She's the overarching goddess of the forge's flames. In addition her sons include the blacksmith god Goibniu, the silversmith god Credne, and the carpenter god Luchta, who would obviously have inherited the Purview from their mom. It's fair not including them on a list of the top tier gods though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T23:59:33-07:00","id":983793,"title":"","content":"Yeah, with that in mind, at my table I might consider replacing &quot;Sun&quot; with &quot;Forge&quot; if my Players make note of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T00:04:29-07:00","id":983797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=983779#post983779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's fair not including them on a list of the top tier gods though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Goibniu is one of the most important gods in the Irish Pantheon.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T00:05:05-07:00","id":983798,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'd make that replacement- I'm unsure why it wasn't that way to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T01:36:48-07:00","id":983823,"title":"","content":"If anybody finds it helpful I made this a while ago:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://app.box.com/s/xmq3sn9x8y0641l8k20dig1vl0zzcw0l\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://app.box.com/s/xmq3sn9x8y0641l8k20dig1vl0zzcw0l\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://app.box.com/s/xmq3sn9x8y0641l8k20dig1vl0zzcw0l\" target=\"_blank\"> https://app.box.com/s/xmq3sn9x8y0641l8k20dig1vl0zzcw0l </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Of course, since I speak modern Irish, this isn't the original Old Irish pronunciation like Scion 2E gives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T15:01:56-07:00","id":984072,"title":"","content":"Does anyone know why Donn has Sky?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T19:23:01-07:00","id":984178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=984072#post984072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know why Donn has Sky?</div> </div> </div> </div>Donn probably has Sky due to being associated with drowning at sea due to storms. Big waves, heavy winds, that sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T12:55:13-07:00","id":985014,"title":"","content":"Brigid not having Forge was a mistake on the part of myself and the author, since it was only decided to be included as a core pantheon rather late.<br /> <br /> Some Gods have more Purviews than others; this is a function of both total Boon investment into Purviews and Legend. Some Gods have the bare minimum for a Purview to be &quot;associated&quot; with them; others have every single Boon in the Purview, and then some. I think, currently, Sun Wukong has a truly ridiculous number of Purviews associated with him, but in the current playtest build this means he doesn't have investment beyond the Demigod level in anything but the Epics, and those just barely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T13:05:57-07:00","id":985021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=985014#post985014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brigid not having Forge was a mistake on the part of myself and the author, since it was only decided to be included as a core pantheon rather late.<br /> <br /> Some Gods have more Purviews than others; this is a function of both total Boon investment into Purviews and Legend. Some Gods have the bare minimum for a Purview to be &quot;associated&quot; with them; others have every single Boon in the Purview, and then some. I think, currently, Sun Wukong has a truly ridiculous number of Purviews associated with him, but in the current playtest build this means he doesn't have investment beyond the Demigod level in anything but the Epics, and those just barely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does a god being highly focused have any positive effects for their scions? Or do the parents associations not matter much beyond that first calling and purview? In 1e there were some gods with barely anything and then gods like Odin and Quetzquatel that had upwards of nine epics and purveiws when you combined them. It made it feel like almost a punishment if you wanted to play a more focused god's scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T13:19:12-07:00","id":985027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=983797#post983797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Goibniu is one of the most important gods in the Irish Pantheon.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's one of the ones mentioned most often, yes. Important?<br /> <br /> Still, if we don't add him in the next draft, Gods are splendidly easy to add.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T13:19:54-07:00","id":985028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=985014#post985014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brigid not having Forge was a mistake on the part of myself and the author, since it was only decided to be included as a core pantheon rather late.<br /> <br /> Some Gods have more Purviews than others; this is a function of both total Boon investment into Purviews and Legend. Some Gods have the bare minimum for a Purview to be &amp;quot;associated&amp;quot; with them; others have every single Boon in the Purview, and then some. I think, currently, Sun Wukong has a truly ridiculous number of Purviews associated with him, but in the current playtest build this means he doesn't have investment beyond the Demigod level in anything but the Epics, and those just barely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does that mean that instead of using Boons for most of his non-epic purviews he has to use Marvel's to achieve similar effects to gods who have boons invested?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T13:20:57-07:00","id":985029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=985021#post985021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does a god being highly focused have any positive effects for their scions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing mechanical besides Path-related effects. You get one Calling, one Purview, that's it - no more no less.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T13:22:07-07:00","id":985030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=985028#post985028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does that mean that instead of using Boons for most of his non-epic purviews he has to use Marvel's to achieve similar effects to gods who have boons invested?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, at a much greater cost and far less efficacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T13:27:23-07:00","id":985033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=985030#post985030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, at a much greater cost and far less efficacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh,thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T13:45:59-07:00","id":985045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=985014#post985014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brigid not having Forge was a mistake on the part of myself and the author, since it was only decided to be included as a core pantheon rather late.</div> </div> </div> </div>...That seems a bit weird to me, 'cause I thought the Tuatha had been slated for the core for a good while now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T14:16:08-07:00","id":985062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=985045#post985045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...That seems a bit weird to me, 'cause I thought the Tuatha had been slated for the core for a good while now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that late in this sense is a relative term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7395-meribson","name":"Meribson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7395_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T14:33:43-07:00","id":985072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=985027#post985027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's one of the ones mentioned most often, yes. Important?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's funny, he's not as important in the old myths, but went on to be practically the only one remembered by modern times in folklore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T14:37:16-07:00","id":985075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=985014#post985014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brigid not having Forge was a mistake on the part of myself and the author, since it was only decided to be included as a core pantheon rather late.<br /> <br /> Some Gods have more Purviews than others; this is a function of both total Boon investment into Purviews and Legend. Some Gods have the bare minimum for a Purview to be &quot;associated&quot; with them; others have every single Boon in the Purview, and then some. I think, currently, Sun Wukong has a truly ridiculous number of Purviews associated with him, but in the current playtest build this means he doesn't have investment beyond the Demigod level in anything but the Epics, and those just barely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, that makes sense. Thanks for speaking up.<br /> <br /> And can I just say that it's REALLY cool that you're willing to regularly pop in to answer questions for us?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T14:43:51-07:00","id":985080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=985045#post985045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...That seems a bit weird to me, 'cause I thought the Tuatha had been slated for the core for a good while now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think he meant &quot;core Purviews&quot;. Forge and Prosperity were originally going to be bonus content.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T16:43:26-07:00","id":985123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=985027#post985027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's one of the ones mentioned most often, yes. Important?</div> </div> </div> </div>Important? Check this out! Goibniu was a badass war hero for one of the most important events in Tuatha history.<br /> <br /> <b>1.</b> When Nuada gives Lugh the Kingship to help with the impending Fomori invasion, Lugh immediately holds a secret meeting for an entire year. Who does he invite? The Dagda, Ogma, <b>Goibniu</b>, and Dian Cecht.<br /> <br /> <b>2.</b> They talk about what they can bring to the war effort. Goibniu makes the most impressive boast -- he guarantees that he will outfit an entire divine army for seven years, replacing every spear that breaks with weapons that &quot;will never miss&quot; and that &quot;no skin which it pierces shall taste life afterwards.&quot;<br /> <br /> Then he talks smack about Dolb, the Fomorian Smith, and points out the enemy smith can't do any of that.<br /> <br /> <b>3.</b> After the fighting starts, the Fomori realize they are losing the entire war for two major reasons. Dian Cecht is going around ressurecting almost everyone who dies on the Tuatha side, and Goibniu is replacing their broken swords, spears, and javelins with super lethal murder versions. In fact, they even talk about him needing only &quot;three turns&quot; / blows to craft a weapon.<br /> <br /> <b>These two almost duohandedly turn the tide of the entire Fomorian war.</b><br /> <br /> <b>4.</b> Ruadan is an assassin and spy for the Fomorians, and he is handed the job of murdering one of the Tuatha. He could have picked anyone, but he decides that Goibniu is the single most important person to the entire war effort. Even over Dian Cecht.<br /> <br /> <b>5</b>. Even more badass? Ruadan gets his hands on one of Goibniu's own murder spears and impales him. Goibniu not only rips it out of his own chest but launches it at Ruadan and kills him with it like something out of a Hollywood action movie. Goibniu then walks off getting impaled and gets healed by Dian Cecht.<br /> <br /> <b>6.</b> I just wanted to throw this in because Irish Mythology has such fun weapons: After the war is won, Goibniu gets sad about his cheating wife and makes Nes, a weapon that causes anyone struck by it to either erupt into boils, or be burned alive like fire.<br /> <br /> <b>7.</b> Some time later, Manannan is trying to help the Tuatha get used to their defeat at the hands of the Milesians. He calls in a favor and asks Goibniu to cook the feast.<br /> <br /> Goibniu always takes things up to 11. So what does he do?<br /> <br /> He creates food and beer that not only make the remaining Tuatha AGELESS but UNABLE TO DIE! Which would have been crazy helpful previously when Nuada got killed, but oh well.<br /> <br /> <b>8.</b> If you like connecting the Tuatha to more modern religious figures, Goibinu continues on as Saint Gobban, or as the folklore figure The Gob\u00e1n Saor.<br /> <br /> The Gob\u00e1n Saor does things like give obscure wisdom to his son to get his son to find a wife through selling a sheep. He builds the world's greatest castle quickly for an English King, tricking the king into sending his heir away to The Gob\u00e1n Saor's house to be kept hostage to make sure nothing nefarious happened to him (it was tradition to kill your architect so they couldn't build anything better for someone else says the story). He built five castles of Kings or great chiefs, could make a spear shaft before you counted to five, <b>make the spear head in three strokes</b>, shows someone how to make a roof if you only have three joists, takes a king's challenge to build a bridge that needs no pegs or nails to hold it together, completing it with a few sticks and a hatchet, with the bridge becoming stronger the more weight that is put on it.<br /> <br /> Definitely one of the heavyweight Tuatha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2273,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","user":"Incendax","date":". 10-10-2016, 08:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T21:14:25-07:00","id":985259,"title":"","content":"Would Cailleach be Tuatha or is she a Fomorian Titan?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T04:39:19-07:00","id":985350,"title":"","content":"Guys, sorry for my bad english but.. i'm an italian scion fan and i love so much this game, so i'm trying to make a step in this community.<br /> <br /> The question is: <br /> <br /> i'm wondering... But metamorphosis for the dodeka isn't too... much? i know, i'm talking without knowing what the purview does but.. I mean, not all the greek gods metamorphs themselves<br /> <br /> If i remember well, just a few of 'em turn into animals or other things. Zeus, first of all, Then, demetra and poseidon... maybe ares with a boar... <br /> <br /> Why aret\u00e9 has been removed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T04:48:13-07:00","id":985353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=985350#post985350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys, sorry for my bad english but.. i'm an italian scion fan and i love so much this game, so i'm trying to make a step in this community.<br /> <br /> The question is:<br /> <br /> i'm wondering... But metamorphosis for the dodeka isn't too... much? i know, i'm talking without knowing what the purview does but.. I mean, not all the greek gods metamorphs themselves<br /> <br /> If i remember well, just a few of 'em turn into animals or other things. Zeus, first of all, Then, demetra and poseidon... maybe ares with a boar...<br /> <br /> Why aret\u00e9 has been removed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there were also instances of them changing other's as punishment, Athena made Medusa a monster as a punishment, arachne was made into a spider for losing a weaving contest to her, Artemis turned a man into a stag for stumbling onto her bathing, I think several people were turned into things like bears or statues for one reason or another. Really the gods do a lot of changing things in greek mythology. And other than &quot;being a jerk&quot; It's really the main trait they all have in common.<br /> <br /> And Arte is probably gone because it was massively OP compared to the other PSPs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T06:25:00-07:00","id":985379,"title":"","content":"Seriously, they shapeshifted themselves and others so much that Ovid could write a whole book about it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T06:34:23-07:00","id":985381,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=985379#post985379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, they shapeshifted themselves and others so much that Ovid could write a whole book about it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> U'r right, i never thoght this<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;And Arte is probably gone because it was massively OP compared to the other PSPs.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Totally Op, in the last edition i used to take the arete revamped, way better","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T08:43:04-07:00","id":985444,"title":"","content":"i really hope that the animal boon will change in a completely different direction. The 1E was really... boring and painfull<br /> <br /> Me and my friends changhed it with some particolar stuff like: The animal who follows you can cast a spell that you prepared before ( silly stuff) like a solar radiance or an healing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T10:42:20-07:00","id":985503,"title":"","content":"My hope is that Geasa is reined in from how it was in the last edition. Ye GODS, nobody needs that many automatic successes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T14:49:19-07:00","id":985694,"title":"","content":"For the thuata i always used &quot;riastradh&quot; and not geasa, so i'm pretty curious","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T15:21:28-07:00","id":985716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=985694#post985694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the thuata i always used &quot;riastradh&quot; and not geasa, so i'm pretty curious</div> </div> </div> </div>The Riastradh... If memory serves, that refers to Cu Chullainn's berserker rage? IIRC, 1E had the Riastradh as an actual Boon of the War Pantheon, as a kind of Super Mode.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I'm curious about the Specific Purviews in general. According to today's update, tomorrow will give us a sneak peek of the Manitou's Specific Purview. Should be fun!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T15:56:20-07:00","id":985739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=985716#post985716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Riastradh... If memory serves, that refers to Cu Chullainn's berserker rage? IIRC, 1E had the Riastradh as an actual Boon of the War Pantheon, as a kind of Super Mode.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I'm curious about the Specific Purviews in general. According to today's update, tomorrow will give us a sneak peek of the Manitou's Specific Purview. Should be fun!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Kinda, the riastradh i used was a fan made i found on the whitewolf wiki<br /> <br /> it allows you to manipulate your body, using your bones like weapon, passing through small passages, became a giant monster<br /> <br /> Stuff like this, pretty cool","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T16:23:35-07:00","id":985762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975383-preview-documents-discussion-thread?p=985123#post985123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>8.</b> If you like connecting the Tuatha to more modern religious figures, Goibinu continues on as Saint Gobban, or as the folklore figure The Gob\u00e1n Saor.</div> </div> </div> </div>An Gob\u00e1n Saor had the posher form in more formal story telling of &quot;Goibhne&quot;, which is even more obviously related to &quot;Goibhniu&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T19:22:24-07:00","id":985887,"title":"","content":"For those who viewed them, I've updated the recordings to include everything from the Tuatha preview:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://app.box.com/s/xmq3sn9x8y0641l8k20dig1vl0zzcw0l\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://app.box.com/s/xmq3sn9x8y0641l8k20dig1vl0zzcw0l\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://app.box.com/s/xmq3sn9x8y0641l8k20dig1vl0zzcw0l\" target=\"_blank\"> https://app.box.com/s/xmq3sn9x8y0641l8k20dig1vl0zzcw0l </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Note:<br /> (a) I'm using Scion's spelling, but my language is over 1,000 years younger. Many words have drifted a long way, although maybe these are the versions modern Scions might hear <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> (b) I translated some of the stuff left in English<br /> (c) Some words are too &quot;Old Irish&quot; for me, there is no surviving descendant word, e.g. Rofhessa, so I left them out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"",